    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup leans heavily on the favorable matchup against Michael Lorenzen and the offensive environment provided by the clash with Seth Lugo. **Dylan Beavers** headlines our starts with a 69.52 efficiency score, bolstered by a strong park factor and a high-leverage spot in the three-hole; while we lose a sliver of value due to Lugo\u2019s ability to hold runners, the overall offensive environment is too potent to ignore. **Taylor Ward** and **Luis Arraez** also provide elite utility at 68.61 and 68.58 respectively. **Arraez** benefits significantly from the SP skill adjustment against Lorenzen, and **Ward** captures a massive park boost that helps him overcome the slight platoon disadvantage. **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Daulton Varsho** round out our high-efficiency group, with **Varsho** currently sitting as a strong play contingent on his assumed #6 spot against Germ\u00e1n M\u00e1rquez, whose 5.58 xERA offers one of the most exploitable windows of the day.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Bryce Harper** on the bench. Despite his elite talent, his 51.36 score was suppressed by a daunting matchup against Tarik Skubal; the optimizer prioritized the higher efficiency of our starters, who face far more favorable arms. **Drew Gilbert** was the next man out, falling just short of the efficiency threshold needed to supplant our outfielders. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Tyler Freeman**, and **Daulton Varsho**, as their official lineups remain pending; should any of these players drop further down the order than projected, their scores will degrade rapidly. Otherwise, we are well-positioned, particularly with **Tyler Freeman** holding the \"slow delivery\" edge, which should provide a slight boost to our pursuit of the league's most scarce category: Stolen Bases.",
